## Operator steps before launch

1. Confirm Hobby eligibility for the intended use. Vercel Hobby is personal/non-commercial; institutional operation needs provider confirmation or a suitable plan.
2. Inspect the Supabase project with hosting/00-inspect-existing-project.sql. Preserve any existing installation and use an empty project for this fresh start.
3. Back up and verify restoration of database and Storage files. The selected-record JSON export is not complete recovery. Free Supabase has no automatic backup entitlement.
4. Run hosting/01-fresh-schema.sql, privately customize/run 02-configure-access.sql, then run 03-private-storage.sql. Do not use legacy default credentials or local seed scripts.
5. Keep ekapon outside the exposed Data API schemas; verify the API role cannot read password hashes or create objects. Keep Storage private without broad anon/authenticated policies.
6. Add the server-only variables from hosting/vercel-env.example.txt to Vercel Production. Use the exact transaction-pooler endpoint and restricted role. Do not share these values or set VITE_ secrets.
7. Use a separate database/bucket/secrets for Preview, or disable Preview. Confirm repository root, production branch and function region before publishing to the connected repository.
8. Resolve/review the two moderate React Router dependency advisories and the recorded account-existence timing behavior. A major dependency upgrade was not silently applied.
9. Supply the official privacy contact/retention rules and approve the Paravet policy before real personal data is entered.
10. Run local checks and then the hosted smoke tests in the guide on an isolated environment. Verify the actual API artifact, authentication, file permissions, exports, cron and provider quotas/availability. Local checks do not establish hosted validation.

